{
  "$comment": [
    "The weapons of D&D 5e. Each key is a weapon the rules know; everything the game does with it comes from here.",
    "name: what it is called. category: simple or martial (who is trained in it, src/data/classes.json). range: melee (STR) or ranged (DEX, shoots at the crosshair).",
    "cost: price in gold (1 sp = 0.1, 1 cp = 0.01; the game's coins are gold only, so a price is paid rounded up to whole gold). weight: kg.",
    "damage: dice such as 1d8 or 2d6, a flat number (1), or null for none; damageType: bludgeoning, piercing or slashing.",
    "distance: [normal, long] range in metres (1.5 m is a 5-foot square of the map): shots fly as far as the long range, rolling with disadvantage past the normal one.",
    "properties: light (fits the second hand for two-weapon fighting, both weapons light), finesse (STR or DEX, whichever is better), thrown, two_handed (no shield or second weapon), heavy, reach (strikes further), loading (one shot per attack, Extra Attack or not), ammunition, special.",
    "versatile: the damage dice when held in both hands (the other hand empty).",
    "art: the item pictures of this weapon in /public/weapons; each is a weapon that can be found. One without art is known to the rules but not found yet."
